# 1) Sequence diagram (Mermaid — paste into README.md or a Markdown file that supports Mermaid)

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant App as Application (main)
    participant HAL as HAL (SPI/UART/GPIO)
    participant ADS as ADS131M08 (SPI device)

    App->>HAL: MX_GPIO_Init(), MX_SPIx_Init(), MX_UART_Init()
    App->>ADS: ADS131M08_Init(handle)
    note right of ADS: ADS131M08_Init() sequence:
    ADS-->>HAL: Toggle RESET pin (HW reset)
    ADS-->>HAL: Send CMD_RESET (SW reset)
    ADS-->>HAL: Send CMD_UNLOCK (allow writes)
    ADS-->>HAL: Write registers: MODE, CLOCK, GAIN1/2, CFG, CHn_CFG...
    ADS-->>HAL: Send CMD_LOCK
    ADS-->>HAL: Send CMD_START (begin conversions)
    App->>HAL: poll DRDY (or wait for EXTI)
    HAL->>App: DRDY = LOW (data ready)
    App->>ADS: ADS131M08_ReadDataFrame(handle)
    ADS->>HAL: SPI transfer: read frame bytes (header + 8×3 bytes [+CRC])
    ADS-->>App: parse 24-bit signed channel samples
    App->>HAL: print samples via UART / store / process
```

And a short ASCII summary:

```
Init sequence:
  - HW reset (RESET pin toggle)
  - CMD_RESET (software)
  - CMD_UNLOCK (allow writes)
  - Write registers (MODE, CLOCK, GAIN1/2, CFG, CHn_CFG...)
  - CMD_LOCK
  - CMD_START (begin conversions)

Runtime:
  - Wait for DRDY (poll or EXTI)
  - On DRDY low -> ADS131M08_ReadDataFrame()
  - Parse header + 8 channels (3 bytes each), optional CRC
  - Convert 24-bit samples to signed int32, process or print
```

