# Integration notes & tips

* Replace the `ADS1_CS_GPIO_Port`, `ADS1_CS_Pin`, `ADS1_RESET_GPIO_Port`, `ADS1_RESET_Pin`, `ADS1_DRDY_GPIO_Port`, `ADS1_DRDY_Pin` macros with the actual macro names CubeMX generated for the pins you used for the ADS instance (same naming convention as in your `main.c` file).
* The test file expects `hspi1` or `hspi2` and `huart1` symbols to be available (as in your existing `main.c`). If you prefer to use SPI2, set `ads.hspi = &hspi2;` and set pins accordingly.
* If your project uses `main()` already, the easiest approach is:

  * Add `ADS131M08_LogAllRegisters()` to your project.
  * After `ADS131M08_Init(&ads1)` call, call `ADS131M08_LogAllRegisters(&ads1);`
* If you have two ADS parts, repeat the logging for `ads2`.

